WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.567
The guided practice combines several patterns.

00:00:02.567 --> 00:00:05.687
We want patients who satisfy four conditions.

00:00:05.687 --> 00:00:10.507
Instead of writing one long query immediately, test each condition separately.

00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:12.692
First the scalar age benchmark.

00:00:12.692 --> 00:00:14.147
Then the admission count. Then abnormal-lab existence.

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:18.782
Then the medication count. Finally, combine the verified conditions with AND.

00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:22.372
For this activity, make a prediction before you run anything.

00:00:22.372 --> 00:00:27.137
State what one output row should represent, which records you expect to remain,

00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:32.017
and what edge case is most likely to expose a mistake.

00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:35.467
Then run the SQL and compare the result with that prediction.

00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:41.037
If it does not match, debug the logic in small pieces instead of changing several clauses at once.

00:00:41.037 --> 00:00:46.212
This is the same habit you would use in a real analytics project: validate the meaning of the result,

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.199
not only whether the statement executes.
